  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Creating new scenes causes the editor console to display a ArgumentException.\nThe exception it self doesn't cause any issues, but it shouldn't be there.\nLooking at the code, this is because the Udon script in question is trying to get scene objects from a invalid scene (just created)\nAdding `if (scene.IsValid()) { }` will remove the exception and still function as normal.\nArgumentException: The scene is invalid.\nUnityEngine.SceneManagement.Scene.GetRootGameObjects (System.Collections.Generic.List`1[T] rootGameObjects) (at C:/buildslave/unity/build/Runtime/Export/SceneManager/Scene.cs:88)\nUnityEngine.SceneManagement.Scene.GetRootGameObjects () (at C:/buildslave/unity/build/Runtime/Export/SceneManager/Scene.cs:75)\nVRC.Udon.Editor.UdonEditorManager.PopulateSceneSerializedProgramAssetReferences (UnityEngine.SceneManagement.Scene scene) (at Assets/Udon/Editor/UdonEditorManager.cs:245)\nVRC.Udon.Editor.UdonEditorManager.OnSceneSaving (UnityEngine.SceneManagement.Scene scene, System.String _) (at Assets/Udon/Editor/UdonEditorManager.cs:238)\nUnityEditor.SceneManagement.EditorSceneManager.Internal_SceneSaving (UnityEngine.SceneManagement.Scene scene, System.String path) (at C:/buildslave/unity/build/Editor/Mono/SceneManagement/EditorSceneManager.cs:68)\nUnityEngine.GUIUtility:ProcessEvent(Int32, IntPtr) (at C:/buildslave/unity/build/Modules/IMGUI/GUIUtility.cs:179)",
